Four libraries OCP depends on have only maintainer skills ("load before editing <dist>"),
none for using them. Cards filed on their boards (see the needs: tags) ask each repo for a
consumer skill. Once one lands:

- `skilletor add <repo> --project` (source name = board name), then
  `skilletor install <skill>@<source> --project`
- brief it into the lane that uses the library:
  - WWW::Hetzner → ocp-provider-worker
  - Crypt::Age, File::SOPS → ocp-secrets-worker
  - Net::Async::Kubernetes → ocp-robocop-worker
- verify with the briefing hook (skill `getty-agent-team`, step 8) — mind the 64 kB soft cap
- commit `.claude/skilletor.json` + the agent files via ocp-release-manager

Rex::Rancher, Rex::GPU and Rex::LibSSH need no card: `rex@getty` covers their use.

